    "text": "A solenoid of inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> has a soft iron core. It is connected to a battery of E.M.F&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> as shown in the figure and allowed to attain its steady state.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"Q.15-16.jpg\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/4f3578c3-0c8e-4d9b-b852-99f5781351b3-image50.jpeg\" style=\"height: 118px; width: 160px;\" /><br />\rAt an instant, the iron core is suddenly pulled out and because of it, inductance decreases to <!--?xml version=\"1.0\"?--> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.<br />\rThe work done by an external agent in pulling out the iron core is",
